{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms","id":1508403,"title":"Has anyone house-ruled lowering the ability requirements of Solar Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-14T18:02:37-07:00","id":1508403,"title":"Has anyone house-ruled lowering the ability requirements of Solar Charms?","content":"Basically thinking about this after a couple of play-throughs. I would really like to lower the ability requirements of multiple Solar Charms so that there were some more spread near the lower range.<br /> <br /> So basically just asking if someone has done something like this already or should I try a quick-fix of having <b>ability min = essence min</b> and see if that works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T06:46:16-07:00","id":1508437,"title":"","content":"The Solar Charmset is a bit... all over the place. Can you perhaps give some examples of where the higher Ability requirements are causing problems at your table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T09:07:23-07:00","id":1508451,"title":"","content":"Yes. I'm a rather vocal proponent of the general idea and all.<br /> <br /> So, the &quot;ability min = Essence min&quot; isn't a horrible starting place, but it goes too far in the opposite direction. The conflict between &quot;Charms are an extension of the character's aptitudes,&quot; and, &quot;you can block a mountain thrown at you with Melee 2,&quot; doesn't really mesh. If every Charm scaled in some fashion to your Ability rating, it would be easily to drop Ability minimums in the first place, because their wouldn't be that disconnect in the first place. If you look at, say, Dragonblooded Excellencies, the difference between Ability 1, and Ability 5 + Specialty is readily apparent in how much you get out of being good at mundane skills reflecting through your Charms (Solars complicate things by their dice-caps being Att+Abl and all). Essence minimums just play into the potency of the Charm (in this example, it's just extra dice, which is good to have but far from world shaking power).<br /> <br /> Without that.. it really becomes an art as you have to weigh all the factors that go into a Charm: does it scale in a fashion, is the effect on the potent side for its Essence rating but justifiable to be available earlier, how many pre-reqs does it have, is the Ability minimum keeping you away from a potential trap because a Charm isn't actually mechanically useful at lower levels, etc.<br /> <br /> Whether you want to start with a really simple thing like abl min = essence min, or some more complicated formula, in the end you're going to be making a lot of individual rules calls (there's a lot of Charms), to the point where you might want to just skip some formula-based quick-fix for not really being as quick as it sounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T13:34:13-07:00","id":1508481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508437#post1508437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar Charmset is a bit... all over the place. Can you perhaps give some examples of where the higher Ability requirements are causing problems at your table?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much an example, I just want charms to be more accessible in general.<br /> <br /> I think 3E went too top heavy on the ability requirements for charms.<br /> <br /> Note: One thing I should probably state, I am also taking away Supernals from Solars. <br /> <br /> To put it simply I want a better sense of progression. (I like starting low and then proceeding to world-breaking power).<br /> <br /> It's hard to do that if Supernals allow you to be the best instantly and ability requirements require you to be one of the best in the world just to get half-way.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> : Thanks for the info. I'll put ability req changes on hold for my next game at least. I am far from mechanically savvy on 3E so I'll try to learn and maybe try one day (and keep my fingers crossed some one does it before that day). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T15:38:01-07:00","id":1508492,"title":"","content":"I think you're overstating Supernals... though it depends a bit on the Ability. While Supernal is a nice bonus, I rarely see players start with more than one or two Essence 3 Charms at max. While you can, in theory, jump up to Essence 5 stuff, you're such a one-trick pony in the process it's the only thing you'll be Exalted-level good at to start. You don't get that many starting Charms after all. After playing some of the other Exalted in 3e, it doesn't really change much, and the longer games go, the less Supernal actually impacts things. While probably a topic for it's own thread, instead of dumping Supernals, consider some other boost that will help set your Solars up to really have an edge in the Ability that's supposed to help define their legend.<br /> <br /> An example of the problem I pointed out in another thread: the Dodge Charms. If you want hand Essence 2 Dodge Charms, you have to have at least Dodge 4, and if you want Essence 3 Charms, you need Dodge 5.<br /> <br /> Lets say you're an Archer and you want Dodge because it gives you some decent Defense and you want to be able to boost your disengage rolls so that you can stay away from opponents. Going beyond the Excellency and getting one Charm to boost your Evasion, and one Charm to boost your disengage, means starting with at least Dodge 4. Dodge 4 is the minimum investing in Dodge to boost your Disengage beyond the Excellency; and not even some of the more potent high level stuff; that's just to get double 9s on one attempt for 2m.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T08:16:31-07:00","id":1508531,"title":"","content":"I had a frustration with the way Ability minimums were distributed until I read the Charm design chapter for Exigents and saw it lay out the idea that it's really about making the bulk of those powers something for the player who is dedicated to that form of capability being part of their character. That the things to characterise somebody as a Solar swordfighter are reserved for the Solar who makes &quot;swordfighter&quot; a specific part of the Solar's legend.<br /> <br /> I think this matters at the macroscopic level where a book is published a bit more than in a balance consideration for where certain Charms go when an individual table can get to them, though.<br /> <br /> Which does kind of bring it down to a simple matter of &quot;if you want some particular Charm without spending the BP or XP to get a 5, then the minimum is whatever your Ability is right now&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T16:41:45-07:00","id":1508580,"title":"","content":"I thought that rationale was fairly evident from the implementation? I know they're dealing with making this work with how the first 3e developers set things up, but it's clear 3e started with the idea of taking a few 5s at start was the default way of things, and there were plenty of public statements about how if you wanted to go from zero to hero than you should clearly appreciate the game making it an actual effort to do so by a specific person.<br /> <br /> I don't think it really simplifies down to &quot;just handwave,&quot; though. Having Ability mins does let you have some fancier powers at lower Essence that do feel like they should be for high Ability characters. I don't think anyone is annoyed by the idea of Heavenly Guardian Defense being a Melee 5 Charm, or that putting it at Essence 2 is good for Melee focused characters so they can get some serious defenses faster. It's things like War Lion Stance jump up to Melee 4 where, yes, it's a solid Charm, but why does &quot;being able to apply Defend Other more easily,&quot; have such a high bar for something far less character defining in terms of the kind of legendary things a Melee focused Solar is going to get up to?<br /> <br /> It also really doesn't address how the rapid jump up in Ability minimums doesn't really leave Charms further down the tree anywhere to go. Anything building off of War Lion Stance has to be 4+, and we're still in the Essence 1 Melee section.<br /> <br /> As I said elsewhere, part of the problem is how 3e defines what Abilities represent. A 3 in Melee is already a battle-hardened veteran. That's already someone that most people think of as a warrior/fighter/gladiator/etc. when thinking about that person's life. It might not be the one defining thing (but then again, that's supposed to be Supernal, not Ability picks, for Solars), but it's certainly an important part of that character as it is. Melee 3 with a specialty in Swords is already someone with renowned swordsmanship. The rather nebulous status of what 4 and 5 mean above that makes how quickly the Charms ramp up to 4 and 5 harder to really make sense of, and harder to implement any sort of hand-wave approach to the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:46:06-07:00","id":1508617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508492#post1508492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAn example of the problem I pointed out in another thread: the Dodge Charms. If you want hand Essence 2 Dodge Charms, you have to have at least Dodge 4, and if you want Essence 3 Charms, you need Dodge 5.<br /> <br /> Lets say you're an Archer and you want Dodge because it gives you some decent Defense and you want to be able to boost your disengage rolls so that you can stay away from opponents. Going beyond the Excellency and getting one Charm to boost your Evasion, and one Charm to boost your disengage, means starting with at least Dodge 4. Dodge 4 is the minimum investing in Dodge to boost your Disengage beyond the Excellency; and not even some of the more potent high level stuff; that's just to get double 9s on one attempt for 2m.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is really my frustration. There is really very little\u200b for someone just wanting to dip in for modest<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508531#post1508531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a frustration with the way Ability minimums were distributed until I read the Charm design chapter for Exigents and saw it lay out the idea that it's really about making the bulk of those powers something for the player who is dedicated to that form of capability being part of their character. That the things to characterise somebody as a Solar swordfighter are reserved for the Solar who makes &quot;swordfighter&quot; a specific part of the Solar's legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is there is a difference between bulk being three+ and making NOTHING be entry level.<br /> <br /> I took a look at the Exigenets Charm Design section (thanks for pointing it out by the way) and then I took a look at the Dodge tree since that was what Heavy Arms used as an example.<br /> <br /> Number of Charms with Dodge 1 Required: ZERO.<br /> Number of Charms with Dodge 2 Required: 1<br /> Number of Charms with Dodge 3 Required: 4<br /> Number of Charms with Dodge 4 Required: 5<br /> Number of Charms with Dodge 5 Required: 16<br /> <br /> Off hand I would have liked one or two charms at Dodge 1 and two or three Dodge 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508531#post1508531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this matters at the macroscopic level where a book is published a bit more than in a balance consideration for where certain Charms go when an individual table can get to them, though.<br /> <br /> Which does kind of bring it down to a simple matter of &quot;if you want some particular Charm without spending the BP or XP to get a 5, then the minimum is whatever your Ability is right now&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said in his post later, it's less about the BP/XP for me, it's more that making those abilities make sense for the character. If two dots in an ability represent a professional which is very likely what my character was before exalting (or became after exalting) then it kinda sucks that there are no options available for them unless he was LEGENDARY in the skill from the get go.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T07:28:54-07:00","id":1508631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508492#post1508492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say you're an Archer and you want Dodge because it gives you some decent Defense and you want to be able to boost your disengage rolls so that you can stay away from opponents. Going beyond the Excellency and getting one Charm to boost your Evasion, and one Charm to boost your disengage, means starting with at least Dodge 4. Dodge 4 is the minimum investing in Dodge to boost your Disengage beyond the Excellency; and not even some of the more potent high level stuff; that's just to get double 9s on one attempt for 2m.</div> </div> </div> </div>So to be clear, I still agree with the overall point. But I think this particular example is worth looking into a just a little bit, because it illustrates something useful: some Charms aren't worthwhile until you hit high Ability ratings anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume that this character, as an Archery specialist who is dipping into Dodge, has Dex 4 and Dodge 2 (as Favored/Caste). For fun, we'll also assume a 1-die stunt on the disengage. This character can expect an average of 3.5 successes on Dex+Dodge+[1d stunt], and can pay 6 motes (max excellency) to average <b>6.5</b> instead.<br /> <br /> Dust Motes Whirling is a Dodge 4/E1 Charm that costs 2m to give you double 9s on a disengage roll. It will cost this character 8 vanilla XP. The character can still expect 3.5 successes on most Dex+Dodge+[1d stunt] rolls, or 6.5 for 6m with max excellency. Without excellency, that's 2m to go from 3.5 to 4.2. Combining both, they can spend up to 8m to average <b>7.8</b>.<br /> \u200b<br /> Going from Dodge 2 to Dodge 4 will cost this character 8 XP of either type. As a result, their average successes on ANY Dex+Dodge+[1d stunt] roll will be 4.5, and they can pay the same 8m to raise it to <b>8.5.</b><br /> <br /> In short, DMW is an icing-on-the-cake (or maybe, &quot;win harder&quot;) Charm. Ability dots and excellency motes are usually (always?) going to be a better deal than a double-whatever or reroll-whatever dice trick, because those Charms make you better in proportion to how good you already are.<br /> <br /> You would only pick up DMW after you have bought all of the other basic bonuses, *if* you want to be <i>the best </i>at Disengage. That's not really Dodge 2 territory; Dodge 4 is probably the earliest it's worthwhile, and that's assuming you've maxed out Dex, have Dodge specialties, have already taken the Fleet of Foot merit, and so on.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508492#post1508492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say you're an Archer and you want Dodge because it gives you some decent Defense and you want to be able to boost your disengage rolls so that you can stay away from opponents. Going beyond the Excellency and getting one Charm to boost your Evasion, and one Charm to boost your disengage, means starting with at least Dodge 4. Dodge 4 is the minimum investing in Dodge to boost your Disengage beyond the Excellency; and not even some of the more potent high level stuff; that's just to get double 9s on one attempt for 2m.</div> </div> </div> </div>So to be clear, I still agree with the overall point. But I think this particular example is worth looking into a just a little bit, because it illustrates something useful: some Charms aren't worthwhile until you hit high Ability ratings anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume that this character, as an Archery specialist who is dipping into Dodge, has Dex 4 and Dodge 2 (as Favored/Caste). For fun, we'll also assume a 1-die stunt on the disengage. This character can expect an average of 3.5 successes on Dex+Dodge+[1d stunt], and can pay 6 motes (max excellency) to average <b>6.5</b> instead.<br /> <br /> Dust Motes Whirling is a Dodge 4/E1 Charm that costs 2m to give you double 9s on a disengage roll. It will cost this character 8 vanilla XP. The character can still expect 3.5 successes on most Dex+Dodge+[1d stunt] rolls, or 6.5 for 6m with max excellency. Without excellency, that's 2m to go from 3.5 to 4.2. Combining both, they can spend up to 8m to average <b>7.8</b>.<br /> \u200b<br /> Going from Dodge 2 to Dodge 4 will cost this character 8 XP of either type. As a result, their average successes on ANY Dex+Dodge+[1d stunt] roll will be 4.5, and they can pay the same 8m to raise it to <b>8.5.</b><br /> <br /> In short, DMW is an icing-on-the-cake (or maybe, &quot;win harder&quot;) Charm. A double-whatever or reroll-whatever dice trick makes you better in proportion to how good you already are. They can still be useful, because they break the dice cap, and for very large dice pools can be more mote-efficient than dice adders too, but they're not for dabblers.<br /> <br /> You would only pick up DMW after you have bought all of the basic bonuses, *if* you want to be <i>the best </i>at Disengage. That's not really Dodge 2 territory; Dodge 4 is probably the earliest it can make sense, assuming you've maxed out Dex, have Dodge specialties, have already taken the Fleet of Foot merit, and so on.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-17-2023, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T09:52:20-07:00","id":1508647,"title":"","content":"I don't think your math really supports what you're conclusion is.<br /> <br /> IF Dex 4/Dodge 2 + stunt + DMW = 4.2 avg successes, and Dex/Dodge 4 + stunt = 4.5, then Dodge 2 sounds like it's exactly where DMW isn't some sort of trap where you should max out all your other Dodge stuff before considering it. And it's not even the &quot;be best at disengage&quot; Charm, it's the first Dodge Charm to boost disengage specifically... more follow. The point here wasn't even to make a &quot;best at Dodge&quot; character, just a &quot;good at Dodge&quot; character to back up being a best at Archery character with some defense that compliments archery. Where you're buying DMW to get some space so you can go back to shooting at a distance as your main way of not getting hit..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T11:37:39-07:00","id":1508656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508647#post1508647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think your math really supports what you're conclusion is.<br /> <br /> IF Dex 4/Dodge 2 + stunt + DMW = 4.2 avg successes, and Dex/Dodge 4 + stunt = 4.5, then Dodge 2 sounds like it's exactly where DMW isn't some sort of trap where you should max out all your other Dodge stuff before considering it. And it's not even the &quot;be best at disengage&quot; Charm, it's the first Dodge Charm to boost disengage specifically... more follow. The point here wasn't even to make a &quot;best at Dodge&quot; character, just a &quot;good at Dodge&quot; character to back up being a best at Archery character with some defense that compliments archery. Where you're buying DMW to get some space so you can go back to shooting at a distance as your main way of not getting hit..</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I threw up a wall of numbers and words; should have been clearer. Here's the TLDR:<br /> <br /> Dex4/Dodge2 + stunt + 2m (DMW alone) = 4.2<br /> Dex4/Dodge4 + stunt + 2m (excel. alone) = 5.5<ul><li>Both options have the same per-action mote cost (2m),</li> <li>Both options have the same XP cost (8xp), but the second can be paid with Solar XP</li> <li>Both have the same per action mote max (8m), but at which the latter is +0.7 successes better on average</li> <li>The first is higher variance (you can only add a success to a die that's already a success)</li> <li>The second one has added +1 avg. success on ALL of their Dodge rolls, not just disengage, for 0 motes forever (and a higher die-added cap on all Dodges)</li> </ul>Dex4/Dodge4 + stunt + 0m = 4.5<br /> <br /> ... which is still better than the DMW option at 2m, for the same XP. At Dex4/Dodge2, you'd be much, much better off buying the 2 Ability dots with your 8 xp <i>even if DMW cost 0m.</i><br /> <br /> DMW is <i>absolutely</i> a trap if you aren't already a Dodge specialist. So again, I'm not disagreeing with the bigger point, there should be something for an Archer who wants to dabble in Dodge to get better at combat movement, but DMW isn't it. I think those Charms ended up in Athletics instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-17-2023, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T12:01:31-07:00","id":1508662,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the cost comparisons really work out, because you can't have DMW without also having the Dodge Excellency. If you have DMW, you have the Excellency for free; and they're not mutually exclusive. You're also very unlikely to be picking these things up with XP because this is some base-line starting Charm selection stuff. &quot;I want some Dodge Charms because I'm making an Archer&quot; means you're going to want to grab a few Dodge Charms with your 15 starters.<br /> <br /> And while, yes, 4.5 &gt; 4.2, that's hardly to the point of being a trap. Maybe it's not the best example because DMW should cost 1m instead or something... but it's splitting a lot of hairs here.<br /> <br /> Also no, Athletics (at least Core Solar Charms) don't have any direct disengage stuff. It has a Charm that can be used after you disengage, and another that lets you make disengage attempts mid-air; neither of which stops you from needing to be good at Dodge to take advantage of. They're the Charms after DMW in the Dodge list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T17:08:51-07:00","id":1508679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508662#post1508662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure the cost comparisons really work out, because you can't have DMW without also having the Dodge Excellency. If you have DMW, you have the Excellency for free; and they're not mutually exclusive. You're also very unlikely to be picking these things up with XP because this is some base-line starting Charm selection stuff. &quot;I want some Dodge Charms because I'm making an Archer&quot; means you're going to want to grab a few Dodge Charms with your 15 starters.<br /> <br /> And while, yes, 4.5 &gt; 4.2, that's hardly to the point of being a trap. Maybe it's not the best example because DMW should cost 1m instead or something... but it's splitting a lot of hairs here</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not 4.5 vs 4.2, it's 5.5 vs 4.2 - in both cases the character *has* the Excellency, the comparison was just a question of which Charm you spend your 2 motes on. The guy who spent 8xp Solar XP on Dodge is 1.3 successes better at Disengage than one who spent 8xp vanilla XP on DMW given that they both spend 2m, but it's even worse because Mr. Dodge4 is *slightly* better at *all* Dodges, without spending motes, than Mr. DMW is at *just* Disengage while spending 2m.<br /> <br /> That all feels pretty Admiral-Akbar to me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T17:20:15-07:00","id":1508682,"title":"","content":"Because you're conflating &quot;the character with more dice rolls better&quot;with it being a trap to buy DMW.<br /> <br /> You're not making the case that DMW being a Dodge 4 Charm is important because if it was less than Dodge 4, characters taking it would be screwing themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T18:52:58-07:00","id":1508701,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I feel like I'm missing something, or else communicating poorly.<br /> <br /> If you have Dodge 2, and your <i>only</i> goal getting the highest average Disengage result you can, AND you have 8xp of <i>any</i> kind to spend, you should still <i>always</i> spend it on Dodge 4. Ignore that &quot;all dodge rolls&quot; &gt; &quot;disengage rolls&quot;. If you have Dodge 2 and <i>every other bonus I can think of:</i><ul><li>Dex 5</li> <li>Fleet of Foot</li> <li>Specialty in &quot;Disengaging&quot;</li> <li>3-die stunt</li> <li>Maxed-out Excellency</li> </ul>Then the benefits of Dodge 4 and DMW are <i>equal</i> (12 average successes for 9m per action). Any less than that and Dodge 4 is just better. For anything other than maximal Disengage, Dodge 4 is <i>way</i> better.<br /> <br /> So yes, I am making the case (or trying?) that putting DMW at Dodge 4 is sensible, because anyone with Dodge less than 4 (and even many with Dodge 4!) should categorically <i>not</i> buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T19:35:02-07:00","id":1508706,"title":"","content":"The problem is that we're not talking about the same goals. Of course if you throw all the creation points/XP at every last thing that boosts disengaging, you'll be better at disengaging,and a bonus like double 9s gets better the more dice you have.<br /> <br /> You're treating &quot;not the most optimal build,&quot; as a a trap, even though this isn't D&amp;D and you're not stuck if you don't buy things in the &quot;best&quot; order. This isn't Ten-Ox Meditation where it is literally never worth using it because the math doesn't work, and buying it is a speed bump if you really want one of the higher-level Athletics Charms that requires pre-req Charms from three different sections of Athletics to get.<br /> <br /> If you want to convince me, here's what I need to hear if you want to make this case:<br /> <br /> 1) DMW actually makes you worse at what it says it's supposed to do (ala TOM)<br /> 2) DMW doesn't help disengage attempts in a meaningful way; I don't care if I can't get 12 successes at Dodge 2, I only want it for situations where 3-5 successes is an adequate average.<br /> <br /> Because we're talking about lowering the mins so that these sorts of Charms are more accessible not because it's optimal. Obviously it's better to have Dodge 4 than Dodge 2. It so that you can make a Dodge 2 or 3 character and still get more of a boost than an Excellency to push you a bit farther when you're willing to throw a lot behind something.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to be forgetting that 3e adds 2 dice to Stunts regardless of level. Higher level stunts add other boosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T19:07:07-07:00","id":1508967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508706#post1508706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we're talking about lowering the mins so that these sorts of Charms are more accessible not because it's optimal. Obviously it's better to have Dodge 4 than Dodge 2.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, and (less obviously?) it's always, in every circumstance, better to have [Dodge 4] than [Dodge 2 + DMW].<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508706#post1508706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It so that you can make a Dodge 2 or 3 character and still get more of a boost than an Excellency to push you a bit farther when you're willing to throw a lot behind something.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is what you're saying that for character reasons, you specifically <i>want</i> to improve disengage <i>without</i> improving Dodge, even if improving your Dodge is a cheaper and universally better way to improve your disengage? Because if so, totally fair, but that would definitely be what I was missing here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508706#post1508706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you seem to be forgetting that 3e adds 2 dice to Stunts regardless of level. Higher level stunts add other boosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch. Habit of a lifetime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T19:35:18-07:00","id":1508973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508967#post1508967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure, and (less obviously?) it's always, in every circumstance, better to have [Dodge 4] than [Dodge 2 + DMW].</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in every circumstance where all other things are equal. But the number of cases where &quot;better&quot; is a fraction of a success better on average is a lot to make so much hay over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So is what you're saying that for character reasons, you specifically <i>want</i> to improve disengage <i>without</i> improving Dodge, even if improving your Dodge is a cheaper and universally better way to improve your disengage? Because if so, totally fair, but that would definitely be what I was missing here. </div> </div> </div>Not just character reasons in some arbitrary sense, but in a verisimilitude sense as well; how the book descriptions of traits informs the desire to give them trait ratings that fits how those characters are envisioned. The desire to want to give a character a rating that makes sense, and not be pressured by the books to go higher for entry level Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T20:39:24-07:00","id":1509131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508973#post1508973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in every circumstance where all other things are equal. But the number of cases where &quot;better&quot; is a fraction of a success better on average is a lot to make so much hay over.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like a success and a half? But to your earlier point, if we're talking about the Difficulty 3-5 range, maybe better to talk about probabilities?<br /> <br /> Mr. Dodge: Dex 4, Dodge 4, Excellency only.<br /> Mr. DMW: Dex 4, Dodge 2, knows DMW and prioritizes using it over Excellency when it applies.<br /> <br /> We'll assume 2 stunt dice, which helps Mr. DMW.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>No mote expenditure:</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>3+ Successes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>4+ Successes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>5+ Successes</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. Dodge (All Dodge)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">88.7%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">75.1%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">57.1%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. DZM (All Dodge)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">77.6%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">57.9%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">37.7%</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2 motes:</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>3+ Successes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>4+ Successes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>5+ Successes</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. Dodge (All Dodge)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">94.4%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">86.3%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">73.1%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. DZM (Disengage)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">84.1%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">70.4%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">53.1%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. DZM (Other Dodge)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">88.7%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">75.1%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">57.1%</td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Maximum motes:</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>3+ Successes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>4+ Successes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>5+ Successes</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. Dodge (All Dodge), <b>8m</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">99.5%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">98.2%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">95.1%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. DZM (Disengage), <b>8m</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">98.4%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">95.8%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">90.8%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mr. DZM (Other Dodge), <b>6m</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">97.4%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">92.7%</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">84.1%</td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd call Mr. Dodge <i>much</i> better, not marginally better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1508973#post1508973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just character reasons in some arbitrary sense, but in a verisimilitude sense as well; how the book descriptions of traits informs the desire to give them trait ratings that fits how those characters are envisioned. The desire to want to give a character a rating that makes sense, and not be pressured by the books to go higher for entry level Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I agree on everything here, except that I'm suggesting DMW isn't an entry level Charm. It's a low-Essence Charm, and a one-prerequisite Charm, but functionally, it makes an already-generally-excellent Solar somewhat better in a narrow circumstance.<br /> <br /> Is there room for an entry-level disengage Charm? Sure. Maybe change the prerequisites and put Shadow Dancer Method first, since it's generally useful to everyone and not just those with really big dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:08:55-07:00","id":1509285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1509131#post1509131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like a success and a half?</div> </div> </div> </div>And you're numbers are still based on a very biased presumption around XP based equivalence (after Dex 4 and Dodge 2) and disregarding char-gen stuff.<br /> <br /> And you're treating &quot;other Dodge&quot; as anything major except for Evasion, which DMW can equal out Dodge 4 with via, Reed in the Wind's dice-cap breaker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You and I agree on everything here, except that I'm suggesting DMW isn't an entry level Charm. </div> </div> </div>You're just goalpost shifting from, &quot;Dodge 4 is important for DMW is important to keep it from being a trap,&quot; to &quot;DMW is really just in the wrong place on the tree.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's an entry level Charm, even if it's a poorly designed one. Frankly, for all the &quot;we basically agree&quot; talk, you're skipping that the problem is that it's a Dodge 4 Charm for the second Charm in a tree, and the first that gives a boost to the second biggest thing Dodge does after Evasion (which the Charm before it does), since the third most is taking cover, which isn't something you have to worry about conflicting against another character over and as long as your ST isn't ignoring the Difficulty guidelines might as well not be a roll most of the time..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T06:05:47-07:00","id":1509472,"title":"","content":"A rule I saw once, which seems to work pretty well, is to reduce Ability mins by 1, unless there\u2019s a prerequisite Charm with a native Ability min of 5. So to use Dodge Charms as an example:<br /> Reed in the Wind becomes Dodge 2, Searing Quicksilver Feint becomes Dodge 3, Force-Stealing Feint becomes Dodge 4, and Seven Shadow Evasion stays Dodge 5 (because FSF is natively Dodge 5).<br /> Also, might I recommend weakening Supernal instead of getting rid of it entirely? Even just allowing it to give +1 effective Essence allows starting characters to have access to cool and flavorful effects, like Glorious Solar Saber or Martial Arts Forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T09:03:02-07:00","id":1509484,"title":"","content":"The &quot;reduce by 1 unless the RAW prereq is a 5&quot; is a decent starting point at least. It still leaves lots of trees really top heavy (it only reduces four Dodge 5 Charms to Dodge 4 Charms for example) It also has weird things the disengage branch still be pretty high Dodge (even if short), while the Reflex Sidestep one suddenly gets very accessible (and I'd argue that Drifting Shadow Focus should stay at a 4 because redirecting attacks at other targets is the kind of stuff that should be gated off for those of exceptional talent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T06:24:38-07:00","id":1509578,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the Combat Abilities probably need a full rework for costs. Starting at 3 dots sacrifices valuable design space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T10:58:14-07:00","id":1509599,"title":"","content":"I&quot;m not sure it's really a combat specific thing. Combat tends to heighten things because it's a more mechanically dense part of the game. Awareness starts at 2, and then jumps to 3+ too. <br /> <br /> Awareness has the advantage of having three distinct branches though, two of which have at least one Awareness 3 Charm (which Sight doesn't is... IDK). But if you just want your character to stick to Awareness 3 but have really good smell, you can have a pretty nice package of both strong utility stuff, and some stand out smell stuff. You can eve go for the Keen (Sense) trio over time if you feel like it. Awareness also has a pretty strong core trunk if you just want all around super-sense for people that are going to want to start with Awareness 5 where you could just bump up the Keen trio, the Unsurpassed trio, and then Awakening Eye and Eyes of the Unconquered Sun. You can get some of the neat tricks in the branches later, but if you just want to go all in on epic super-senses, you can to that too. The more combat-focused Abilities tend to be either really lopsided in what they offer (Dodge has tons of support of Evasion, but minimal for doing much with combat movement), or multiple trees that co-mingle in the branches; so there isn't that balance of a decent package for people that only want a small part of the whole and a core trunk of all-around super-competence (though Craft as the same problem).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:43:43-07:00","id":1509656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1508403-has-anyone-house-ruled-lowering-the-ability-requirements-of-solar-charms?p=1509472#post1509472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rule I saw once, which seems to work pretty well, is to reduce Ability mins by 1, unless there\u2019s a prerequisite Charm with a native Ability min of 5. So to use Dodge Charms as an example:<br /> Reed in the Wind becomes Dodge 2, Searing Quicksilver Feint becomes Dodge 3, Force-Stealing Feint becomes Dodge 4, and Seven Shadow Evasion stays Dodge 5 (because FSF is natively Dodge 5).</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds rather nice. I think I'll use it.<br /> <br /> One house rule I was thinking of before this was also to allow players who bought an excellency in a non-favored ability which had 0 charms at Ability level 1 , to automatically get a free charm in that ability at level 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1424_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1424\" data-vbnamecard=\"1424\">GhanjRho</a>'s rule is better but I just wanted to toss this out there.<br /> <br /> Also I found this in a <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/e61cv7/complaint_topheavy_skill_requirements_for_charms/\" target=\"_blank\">reddit thread</a> but I thought it might be useful for this topic:-<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_s6JZe6869f81l9E_5G7Q9 text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_s6JZe6869f81l9E_5G7Q9 text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv_tr\"><td class=\"text_table__3DYfYn_cczg1wj_a3hhyV6 text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv_td text_table_s6JZe6869f81l9E_5G7Q9_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 5px\">Archery</td> <td class=\"text_table__1LHijgw3WoeCUe8AUewfUB text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv_td text_table_s6JZe6869f81l9E_5G7Q9_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 5px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table__1LHijgw3WoeCUe8AUewfUB text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv_td text_table_s6JZe6869f81l9E_5G7Q9_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 5px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table__1LHijgw3WoeCUe8AUewfUB text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv_td text_table_s6JZe6869f81l9E_5G7Q9_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 5px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table__1LHijgw3WoeCUe8AUewfUB text_table_MRH-njmSb5ZTkfb1o4dqv_td text_table_s6JZe6869f81l9E_5G7Q9_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; p