or: #B45F06; border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">279</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #FF00FF; border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">59</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #FF00FF; border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">39</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T11:42:36-07:00","id":1536313,"title":"","content":"IMO: Solar charms being weighted towards five makes sense in a way. You're not playing &quot;Joe Bob the human fighter&quot; for whom average stats are a wonderful thing, you're playing &quot;Golden Sun Before Whom Gods Bow.&quot; If you want to be supernaturally good at something, the game expects you to also be actually good at it. After all, the exalted are exceptional people. <br /> <br /> Now it is possible the developers went too far in that direction. There's also only so many points at character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T22:44:31-07:00","id":1536330,"title":"","content":"Without retread the whole thread:<br /> <br /> Nobody actually disagrees that the Ability minimums have a place to emphasize unique talent and high level effects going hand-in-hand. Heavenly Guardian's Defense should be a Melee 5 Charm.<br /> <br /> The problem is that there's no consistency to this. For all the talking-past-each-other debates around the mechanical value of Dust Motes Whirling... why does double 9s on a single disengage roll (which isn't even a guarantee of doing better, just an odds booster) belong at the level of being one of the best in a whole Direction at escaping combat?<br /> <br /> Dice tricks and other things that aren't obviously supernatural actions being behind the 4+ Ability wall detracts from those Charms that should be that highly rated being special. You should see an Ability 4 or 5 Charm and be able to trust you're getting something that you might not use all the time, but when you do it should be awesome, but instead it could be anything from an underwhelming dice-trick, to awe-inspiring display of divine excellence. So players aren't being trained to use Ability minimums are a guide to what sort of Charm to expect, just what sort of hoops the Charm is expecting you to jump through.<br /> <br /> When &gt;60% of the Charms are Ability 5 Charms, I'm pretty sure we're well beyond things having possibly gone too far. If the ratio of Charms was 1:2:3:4:5, so there's five Ability 5 Charms for each Ability 1 Charm, there would be ~57 Ability 1 Charms (which would still be only 2-3 Charms per Ability), not 23, and ~285 Ability 5 Charms, not 536. The weighting is intensely towards 5s in a fashion that's hard to excuse as good design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T10:54:36-07:00","id":1536571,"title":"","content":"Agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, <br /> <br /> Issue is not so many Ability 5 charms.<br /> <br /> Issue is lack of Ability 1 and 2 charms.<br /> <br /> Some Abilities lack any charms for those levels, making them effectively 'dead' ability levels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T19:46:33-07:00","id":1540192,"title":"","content":"<br /> Likewise trying not to retread. I still stand by what me-from-last-year said about how some Charms, as written, belong at A4-5 because of mechanical nuance rather than vibe. But maybe I can try to say it a different (better?) way.<br /> <br /> As game system components, I postulate that Charms in Exalted serve a couple of different purposes. They layer on top of the &quot;mortal rules&quot; in two ways:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Access effects that are outside that framework but resonate with the character type. The lines starting with Call the Blade and Whirlwind Armor-Donning Prana are good archetypal examples.</li> <li>Allow continued advancement past where the core mechanics stop. For an archetype here I would point to Excellencies or to Iron Whirlwind Attack.</li> </ol>That's not to say that any given Charm couldn't or shouldn't be both; just that spending XP is &quot;advancement&quot; along these two orthogonal vectors of &quot;forward&quot;.<br /> <br /> The two types relate differently to the three styles of prerequisites: Ability, Essence, and Antecedent Charms.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>For a Charm to make &quot;Type 1 sense&quot; mostly you need the right Antecedents (page 254 of Ex3 calls this &quot;coherence&quot;). The steps you take as you walk further from mundanity have to make sense. You need Essence to set the right tone of &quot;how supernatural is this&quot;, but Ability is just an anchor to say &quot;how invested in this Ability must you be for it to make sense in a Solar context&quot;. Is this something a farmhand or scholar or merchant with only rudimentary combat skill who finds himself invested with Solar Power should be able to do [Melee 1]? An exceptional professional combatant [Melee 3]? An already-legendary (for a mortal) master of swordsmanship?</li> <li>For a Charm to make &quot;Type 2 sense&quot;, prereqs are about finding the point where the Charm is better/different than the core mechanical advancement. In the Solar case, when would you fork off of advancing the Ability itself to get this effect if you're interested in it. Is it &quot;Ability 6&quot;? &quot;Ability 2b&quot;? Then antecedents allow these forks to keep progressing laterally (away from the core) or vertically (past maxed out Ability/Attribute), while Essence brackets &quot;how far into the game should you be before you can advance this way&quot;.</li> </ol>This creates some different design spaces, and I think it explains <i>some</i> of the distribution &quot;problems&quot; cited above. To make sense at Low Ability, you need to be only somewhat dependent on the &quot;legendary swordsman/thief/captain/whatever&quot; angle of Solar theming if Type 1 (e.g. Call the Blade) AND be a logical parallel advancement track even at low Ability if Type 2 (e.g. Excellencies, Wise Arrow). But because <i>being a master [X]</i> is so close to Solar theming you're not going to see many Type 1s below Ability 3. It's a little easier to come up with Type 2s that low but even then much of the time a niche bonus is wasted on someone who doesn't have decent competence. Learn to walk before you try running.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, I think it's a mistake to think of Ability prereqs as though they're a five-tier scale for Charm power. I think it's <i>more</i> helpful to think of each Ability dots as integrated into the tree like Charms themselves, and yeah, <i>most</i> Charms don't branch off until the third, fourth, or fifth dots. Charms are a big tech tree of which Ability and Essence are a part. In the Solar case, Abilities form the root <i>and</i> trunk of the tree and most Charms are the upper branches.<br /> <br /> So looking back at DMW, the effect as written is pure Type 2. It advances a niche application of Dodge, in the <i>same way</i> as advancing Dodge (higher probability of success). So the logical point to fork off is when it might be a meaningful advancement choice - i.e. when you have a sufficient dice pool that DMW outperforms general advancement <i>within its niche</i>, and I think Dodge 4 is as close as you get there. Otherwise, it's a false choice. Personally I <i>would</i> remove the antecedent Charm though because it <i>doesn't</i> advance Reed in the Wind in any meaningful way, so RitW is an inappropriate Type 2 prerequisite.<br /> <br /> But is DMW a good Charm? No. A one-roll niche double-9s isn't interesting or powerful effect to carry a whole Charm, even if Ability 4 is a good min for that <i>part </i>of the effect. Dice tricks make better riders for higher-Ability Charms with other effects than they do stand-alones. For one example of what this Charm<i> could </i>have been instead, see Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise. Same mins, gives double-9s on a single roll in a specific Larceny niche - disguise - but also gives two auto successes, and layers on three other benefits: enabling completely illogical disguises, protecting against non-magical senses, and making the Solar herself unrecognizable even if you do see through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 08-12-2024, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}